WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.622
This table summarizes the text half of the module.

00:00:02.622 --> 00:00:05.757
Use the simplest function that matches the actual problem.

00:00:05.757 --> 00:00:08.812
Do not use regex when TRIM solves the issue.

00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:13.802
Do not use fixed positions when a reliable delimiter defines the structure.

00:00:13.802 --> 00:00:19.152
And do not treat cleaning as proof of validity.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.907
Clear, small transformations are easier to maintain and explain.

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:27.277
Connect this idea to a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:32.222
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:32.222 --> 00:00:38.807
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.807 --> 00:00:43.897
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:49.120
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
